  "verdict": "WIN",
  "verdict_basis": "at every completed size the symmetrized full system solves at visibly lower degree and time WITH membership encoded (driven by the S3-orbit collapse: quotient dimension ~6x smaller); divergence: original censored at 14_32 (> 150s) while symmetrized completes at 14_64 (89.5s)",
  "caveats": [
    "Toy regime: varieties are tiny (planted decomposition plus a handful of accidental ones); the GBs are structure-driven, not ECDLP-scale solves. At the ECDLP-relevant |F| = l^(1/3) BOTH formulations are hopeless (membership degree ~ l^(1/3)).",
    "The measured advantage is a HORIZONTAL SHIFT of an exponentially growing trajectory (original: 0.05s,0.47s,5.6s,>150s at |F|=8,12,16,32; symmetrized: 0.0016s,...,89.5s at |F|=8..64), driven by the S3-orbit quotient (~6x smaller quotient dimension) \u2014 a formulation-quality win, NOT an exponent change.",
    "Membership-in-e encoding grows ~ |F|^3 monomials in 3 shared variables (17 -> 951 -> 8099 at |F| = 8,32,64) vs 3 univariate degree-|F| polys; it does not kill the symmetrized system at these sizes, but it is why the sym curve also blows up (wall near |F| ~ 96-128 extrapolated, vs ~ 20-30 for the original).",
    "Single instance per size (fixed seed); the >150s original censoring at |F|=32 is an alarm-bound measurement, consistent with the monotone 10x-per-doubling trend.",
    "'max degree' = max total degree of the final degrevlex GB basis; the F4/F5 solving degree trajectory is not directly instrumented.",
    "Quotient dimensions count points WITH multiplicity; the ~6x collapse matches the S3 orbit at non-degenerate sizes (6 vs 1 at 16_16; 12 vs 2 at 14_12)."
  ]
